## 4. Domains eliminated by default

| Domain/risk family | Why eliminate by default | Acceptable exception |
|---|---|---|
| Cybersecurity/cryptography/dark web | Requires attacker models, secure engineering, adversarial testing, forensic validity, and specialist data. | Narrow offline log analyzer or compliance checklist with a security mentor. |
| Medical diagnosis/mental-health prediction | Requires clinical validation, privacy, bias controls, and safety review. | Non-diagnostic workflow, education, or referral assistant. |
| Weather/disaster prediction | Requires calibrated scientific models, multi-source data, false-alarm handling, and operational validation. | Visualization, alert explanation, or simulator. |
| Satellite/ocean/space science | Requires remote-sensing data, scientific modelling, and validation. | Image exploration/search/segmentation proof of concept. |
| Autonomous robotics/vehicles/drones | Requires sensors, simulation, real-time control, safety, and field testing. | Planning simulator or offline route optimization. |
| Quantum/quantum-inspired claims | Requires algorithmic expertise and classical baselines; advantage claims are difficult to prove. | Educational simulator or classical-vs-quantum comparison. |
| Defense/electronic warfare | Requires restricted/specialized data, domain knowledge, and safety/security controls. | Do not select without authorized expert support. |

