## 7. AI suitability: what is genuinely feasible

| AI capability | Good use | Avoid claiming |
|---|---|---|
| LLM assistant | FAQs, onboarding, report guidance, summarization, natural-language search. | Official legal/medical/security advice or autonomous action. |
| OCR/document extraction | Read labels, forms, invoices, IDs, and compliance fields. | Perfect extraction without human review. |
| Image classification | Suggest waste type, crop disease class, quality grade, or document category. | Diagnostic certainty or unsupported confidence. |
| Similarity/deduplication | Find related complaints, documents, or records. | Identity attribution or criminal certainty. |
| Anomaly detection | Flag unusual logs, sensor values, or transaction patterns. | Guaranteed threat/fraud detection. |
| Prediction/recommendation | Prioritize work, suggest routes, or recommend next action. | Guaranteed weather, disease, crime, or safety prediction. |
| Translation/speech | Vernacular help, voice input, accessibility. | Perfect translation for high-stakes instructions without review. |

## 8. Selection scorecard

Score each candidate from 1–5 before choosing. A high total with no critical blocker is preferable to a flashy but unverifiable idea.

| Criterion | Question | Weight |
|---|---|---:|
| Problem fit | Does it directly answer the official statement? | 5 |
| Data availability | Can we obtain representative data or use an authorized public dataset? | 5 |
| End-to-end buildability | Can we show the full workflow without manual intervention? | 5 |
| AI leverage | Does AI add useful assistance rather than decoration? | 3 |
| Validation | Can we measure quality and failure cases? | 4 |
| Integration risk | Are APIs, hardware, permissions, or deployment under control? | 4 |
| Domain safety | Can we make claims responsibly? | 4 |
| Demo clarity | Will a judge understand value in five minutes? | 5 |

## 9. Recommended strategy for your team

First shortlist three statements from workable domains. For each, create a one-page concept containing the user, current pain, input data, core workflow, AI role, database entities, measurable output, demo scenario, and risks. Reject a candidate if you cannot name the dataset, first user, success metric, and fallback behaviour.

For CleanTrack specifically, verify the exact official problem ID because the workbook’s Clean & Green rows are different from the earlier civic-dumping brief. If CleanTrack is from another official list, use the exact matching ID and wording in the final submission.

## 10. Caveats

The spreadsheet’s “Submitted Idea(s) Count” values are not used as a measure of competition or difficulty. Difficulty and feasibility here are analytical estimates based on the statement titles, domains, likely dependencies, and typical student-team constraints. The simplified translations are intended for team understanding, not as replacements for the official wording in a submission.

